   "conversationId": "2102695007404822995",
   "text": "Young brains need civilizational grounding, and Kannada textbooks provided that. In the above example, I had learnt that the real names of Everest are Sagarmatha and Chomolungma instead of anchoring myself in the farce that \"Everest discovered Everest\".\n\n30 years later, as I train a newer version of AI on the corpus of medical literature, I wonder if the same principles worked in making us utter nonsense like parrots because the entire education was hijacked by colonial vestiges which produce dumbo like Ruchika Sharma who has a doctorate and does not even know anything! \n\nAt least vernacular languages did not have so much fakeness because the lived history was strong.",
