   "conversationId": "2102751520697757817",
   "text": "I think it is important to understand that template of right/conservative movement in the USA can not be applied to India.\n\nThe Federalist Society can happen only when there is critical reasoning.   \n\nIn India, critical reasoning has been totally removed through a century or more of fake narratives being fed en masse, creating what I call \"anchoring bias\".\n\nHumanities in India are really not human insights. They are most toxic narratives which are taken as gospel truth and most of the fakery of colonialism is brushed aside with fictitious claims on caste and other things brought by the colonizers. \n\nThis was the only study Indians were allowed after the Hindu school system was decimated, plunging India into material as well as spiritual poverty. \n\nSo asking why India has not produced a \"right leaning\" institution is wrong question. \n\nBharat had pramana based teaching where both left, right, center could figure out correct world view. This is what has been removed with toxic @incindia and its Nehru invader culture. \n\nI wish I had more time today to pen a detailed response.",
