   "conversationId": "2102765773819375754",
   "text": "Alta's use is mentioned in Natyashastra. It is still used. \nThe hands and feet are colored with alta to highlight the intricate hand gestures during various mudras\n\nHenna is sometimes used instead of Alta by modern Bharatnatyam dancers who are also working in corporate jobs because henna is not very staining. You can still shake hands with clients, whereas Alta stains very dark and unless you keep applying a newer coat.\n\nHenna is actually described in Sushrutha Samhita  (medical text dating back to BCE)",
